<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Guangzhouwan</h1><p class="st-meta">1898 CE – 1945 CE · capital Fort-Bayard</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small French leased territory on the coast of Guangdong, administered as part of French Indochina for nearly half a century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>During the scramble for concessions in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> occupied the bay of Guangzhouwan on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leizhou-peninsula">Leizhou</a> peninsula in 1898, and a convention of 1899 granted it a ninety-nine-year lease. France wanted a coaling station and a counterweight to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hong-kong-british">British Hong Kong</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The territory was attached to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/french-indochina">French Indochina</a>, governed by an administrator under the governor-general in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a>, with its seat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhanjiang">Fort-Bayard</a> (modern Zhanjiang). It never became the great port <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> hoped for, and its economy rested on local trade, a free port, opium and smuggling. Local Chinese notables kept much influence over daily life.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> occupied the territory in 1943 with the acquiescence of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vichy-france">Vichy France</a>. In August 1945 the French provisional government agreed to return it, and it passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nationalist-government">Nationalist government</a> in the following months, becoming the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhanjiang">Zhanjiang</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/guangzhouwan.jpg" alt="Guangzhouwan" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: noUSERname · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Colonial_Annam.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1898 CE – 1945 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Fort-Bayard</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Chinese folk religion, Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Cantonese, Leizhou Min, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>China</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kouang-Tcheou-Wan, Fort-Bayard</dd></dl></aside></div>
